Designing a globally distributed, multi-region order-matching engine (OME) with **strict serializability**, **sub-millisecond execution**, and **Disaster Recovery (RPO = 0, RTO < 5s)** requires an architecture that bridges high-frequency trading (HFT) microsecond-level determinism with globally distributed consensus.

### 1.1 Architectural Overview

